{
  "as_of": "2026-10-31",
  "purpose": "Tests whether Talnaspor understands questions it was not written for: paraphrases and synonyms, restrictions (sex, region, age), change over time on catalog tables, follow-up questions, and questions that must not be answered. Written on 2026-10-31, before the changes they measure.",
  "rules": "The 'dev' split may be used while developing rules and prompts. The 'holdout' split must not be: it is scored only at checkpoints (the baseline, after each task, and the LLM go/no-go decision), and only its totals are reported. Each 'accept' entry is a table cell (or two, for a comparison) that correctly answers the question; its values are fetched by scripts/fetch_expected.py, which shares no code with Talnaspor. An answer is correct when its value (both values, for a comparison) and its period match an accepted entry. 'kind' says how a comparison's change is stated: percentage points for a percent, a percent change for an index, and both the difference and the percent change for a count. 'ambiguous' marks a question where more than one category plausibly matches; there a clarification is as good as an answer that states the category. 'previous' is the question a follow-up refers to.",
